@startuml
title DFNS Admin Key Setup and Policy Configuration\n(Privileged Role Wallet Provisioning — Full Cloud Deployment)
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam wrapWidth 460
autonumber

box "R3 Security / Admin" #LightYellow
actor "Security Admin\n(R3)" as Admin
actor "Protocol Config\nAuthority" as PCA
end box

box "R3 Internal Systems" #LightBlue
participant "Admin UI\n(Browser)" as UI
participant "Admin BFF\n(Server)" as BFF
participant "Secret Manager\n(Azure Key Vault)" as SecMgr
end box

box "External Identity Provider" #LightCyan
participant "Microsoft Azure AD\n(Entra ID)" as AAD
end box

box "DFNS Cloud (External)" #LightPink
participant "DFNS API\n(Org Management)" as DFNS
participant "DFNS MPC Network\n(Key Gen Nodes)" as MPC
end box

box "Backup / Redundancy Layer" #LightGreen
participant "Squads V4\n(External M-of-N Multisig)" as Squads
actor "R3 Hardware Key\nHolders (M-of-N)" as HWHolders
participant "High-Availability\nWallet (Emergency)" as HAWallet
end box

== Phase 1: DFNS Organisation Setup ==

Admin -> DFNS: Create DFNS organisation\n(R3 tenant, full cloud deployment)
Admin -> AAD: Configure Azure AD OIDC application\n(federate to DFNS as identity provider)
DFNS --> Admin: Organisation created\n{orgId, rootServiceCredential}

note over SecMgr #PaleGreen
**CONTROL: Secret Manager Storage (DFNS_CRED_IN_SECRETS_MANAGER)**
Root service credential stored immediately in Azure Key Vault.
IAM policy: BFF service identity read-only; no human access.
Audit logging enabled on all retrieval events.
end note

Admin -> SecMgr: Store DFNS service credential\n(API key + private key)\nIAM: BFF managed identity only

== Phase 2: Privileged Wallet Provisioning ==

note over Admin, MPC
**For each privileged protocol role:**
Curator, Vault Manager, Protocol Manager,
Protocol Config Authority, Vault Guard, ACL Authority
end note

Admin -> DFNS: POST /wallets\n{name: "Curator Wallet", network: "Solana"}
DFNS -> MPC: Generate MPC key shares\n(Ed25519, Solana-compatible)
MPC --> DFNS: Public key returned\n(key shares distributed across nodes)
DFNS --> Admin: Wallet created\n{walletId, publicKey: <Base58>}

note over DFNS #MistyRose
**RISK: DFNS Insider (DFNS_INSIDER_KEY_SHARE_ABUSE)**
Key shares are distributed at this step.
A DFNS insider could interfere with key generation.
**Mitigation:** Verify generated public key matches expected format.
**Mitigation:** Validate SOC2 attestation covers key generation procedures.
end note

== Phase 3: Signing Policy Configuration ==

Admin -> DFNS: Configure signing policy for Curator wallet:\n- Require WebAuthn approval: YES (for config ops)\n- Allowed operations: settle_deposits,\n  settle_redemptions, pause_vault\n- Alert on policy change: YES
Admin -> DFNS: Configure signing policy for Protocol Config Authority:\n- Require WebAuthn approval: YES (mandatory)\n- Allowed operations: admin instructions only\n- Spending limit: N/A (non-financial role)

note over DFNS #MistyRose
**RISK: Policy Misconfiguration (DFNS_POLICY_MISCONFIGURATION)**
Permissive policy (no WebAuthn, no operation filter) removes
the DFNS layer as a safeguard.
**Mitigation:** Security Admin review of each policy before go-live.
**Mitigation:** Alert webhook on any future policy change.
end note

Admin -> DFNS: Register WebAuthn credential for each role holder\n(FIDO2 hardware key — separate from SSO key)
DFNS --> Admin: WebAuthn credential registered

note over Admin #PaleGreen
**CONTROL: WebAuthn Independent of SSO (DFNS_WEBAUTHN_SEPARATE_FROM_SSO)**
Each role holder registers a dedicated FIDO2 key for DFNS approvals,
separate from their Azure AD FIDO2 key.
SSO session compromise cannot be used to approve DFNS signing.
end note

== Phase 4: External Redundancy Setup (Critical Roles) ==

note over Admin, HWHolders
**For upgrade authority and protocol config authority only:**
These keys must NOT rely solely on DFNS.
(Ref: DFNS_UPGRADE_KEYS_EXTERNAL_MULTISIG countermeasure)
end note

Admin -> Squads: Create external M-of-N Squads multisig\n(e.g., 3-of-5 for upgrade authority)
HWHolders -> Squads: Register R3-owned hardware wallet keys\n(Ledger / Keystone — physically held)
Squads --> Admin: Multisig PDA created\n{multisigAddress}

note over Squads #PaleGreen
**CONTROL: External Redundancy for Critical Keys**
Upgrade authority transactions must pass through this Squads multisig.
Even if DFNS is fully compromised, attacker cannot execute upgrades
without M-of-N approval from R3-held physical keys.
end note

== Phase 5: Emergency Halt Key Setup ==

Admin -> HAWallet: Provision Security Halt key on\nhigh-availability wallet\n(outside DFNS — e.g., mobile Ledger Live)
Admin -> HAWallet: Configure push notifications:\n- Alert on pending time-locked actions\n- NCC SOC integration for monitoring

note over HAWallet #PaleGreen
**CONTROL: Emergency Halt Redundancy (DFNS_EMERGENCY_HALT_REDUNDANCY)**
Vault pause key available independently of DFNS.
If DFNS is unreachable, Security Halt can still be executed
from this wallet without DFNS signing.
end note

HAWallet --> Admin: Emergency halt key ready\n(veto key also provisioned here)

== Phase 6: On-Chain Role Assignment ==

PCA -> BFF: Assign on-chain role:\n"Set Curator to <DFNS Curator wallet pubkey>"
BFF -> DFNS: Sign vault config transaction\n(using Protocol Config Authority DFNS wallet)
DFNS --> BFF: Signed transaction
BFF -> Squads: Submit via Squads timelock\n(routes through Squads for timelock enforcement)
Squads --> BFF: Proposal created\n(timelock window begins)

note over Squads #PaleGreen
**CONTROL: Timelock Integration (DFNS_TIMELOCK_INTEGRATION)**
All protocol config changes submitted via Squads timelock.
Veto window: configured timelock period.
Veto key held on HA wallet (Phase 5) independent of DFNS.
end note

== Phase 7: Audit Baseline ==

Admin -> DFNS: Export initial policy configuration snapshot\n(wallets, policies, WebAuthn registrations)
DFNS --> Admin: Configuration export\n{JSON/CSV snapshot}
Admin -> SecMgr: Store policy snapshot in immutable log store\n(Azure Sentinel — baseline for drift detection)

note over Admin #PaleGreen
**CONTROL: Audit Log Integrity (DFNS_AUDIT_LOG_INTEGRITY)**
Baseline policy snapshot preserved outside DFNS.
Periodic drift checks compare live DFNS config against baseline.
Alert on any deviation from approved policy state.
end note

@enduml
